If a patient has a subacute-pain then every clinician should reevaluate the patient.
If a patient has a subacute-pain then every clinician should reevaluate a treatment-course for the patient.
If a patient has a subacute-pain then every clinician should address a potentially-reversible-ongoing-pain-cause for the patient.
If a patient has a subacute-pain and a pain-management-optimization is needed for the patient then every clinician should optimize a pain-management for the patient.
